  "chain": "DUB-17 Theorem 2.6 / DUB-18 Corollary 8.2 -> literal higher symmetric-power continuation -> arithmetic automorphy -> original all-weight characteristic-zero association -> original Gamma1 Tate/Frobenius realization -> actual coordinate degree/genus preservation -> signed-index lower bound -> reduced field action -> level-power slash integrality -> even-weight peaked auxiliary existence.",
  "selectedNext": "Prove the exact finite Bernoulli-weight separation using native Bernoulli Fourier series, finite Fourier inversion and the already proved Mathlib nonvanishing of Dirichlet L-series at 2. Construct the source nonnegative integer exponent family. The actual Siegel product, transformation, Fourier integrality and leading-unit comparison remain separately required.",
  "sourceScope": "The source exponent family is invariant under (r,s) -> (r,s+r), excludes (0,0), and separates precisely the two exceptional signed cusp classes on unimodular columns. The actual modular form is the product of Siegel functions to 12*N*m(r,s), multiplied by a power of the original discriminant, of weight 12*t.",
  "shorterRoutes": {
